{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPmmAz2MeQajDSVCtd6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gp4Ya9UqYUoqEwPvH6Xgm8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\ndef sub(f,a,b):\n    s=open(f).read(); assert a in s,(f,a); open(f,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('docs/proposal.md','The merger, prwatch and scanners are never woken this way.','The merger, prwatch and scanners are never woken this way. Hand-offs wake the next loop too (#406): after its label effects succeed, a close-out wakes the loops that now have work (`ard:worker:<role>` wakes workers; `ard:review:<role>` reviewers; `ard:triage:<role>`, `ard:pending` and a triage `:done` label triage, whose fan-in gate adds the worker label; a review `:done` the merger; a review `:changes` reviewfix and workers), through the same debounced per-loop wake, logged as `controller.wake reason=closeout`. A failed, retried, stale or needs-human close-out wakes nothing, and dry-run wakes nothing. A human approval comes from GitHub, so ard polls for it: the approval watch is a controller loop that takes no slot and runs no agent. Every `intervals.approvals` (default and minimum 1m) it makes three searches (`ard:approved`, `ard:needs-human`, `ard:executor:failed` on open items). An approved item with no worker label wakes triage (`reason=approval`); an item that was blocked on the previous poll and no longer is wakes the loops that own it (`reason=unblocked`; the watch keeps the blocked set in memory, so a removal during a restart is left to the loops\\' own intervals). The woken loop does the real check: the triage gate still requires the approval to come from an allowed actor after triage finished, so a rejected approval starts no worker. A paused controller skips the watch and runs nothing on a wake. The full triage poll keeps its own interval.')\nsub('docs/proposal.md','merger: 5m, prwatch: 5m }','merger: 5m, prwatch: 5m, approvals: 1m }')\nsub('docs/site/configuration.md','| `pr_watch.pending_timeout`','| `intervals.approvals` | `1m` | Approval watch poll (minimum `1m`): one cheap search for a human adding `ard:approved` or removing `ard:needs-human` or `ard:executor:failed`; a hit wakes the loop that owns the item, so the triage interval can stay long |\\n| `pr_watch.pending_timeout`')\nE\nmake lint test 2>&1 | grep -v \"redact.log\\|^ok\\|no test files\" | tail -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3104,"cache_read_input_tokens":95950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3104},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9504e90-0a46-4f9b-9664-2e88cac7e920","uuid":"42321c4d-0299-4e51-9aa5-1d52ee875b32","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:04:30.930Z","request_id":"req_011ChPmmAqLaUK8yjjixQimz"}
