{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPnAj7SkCdWyqiBvuSWf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Close-out now wakes the loops that have new work, and a new approval watch wakes the loop that owns an item when a human approves or unblocks it. `make lint test` passes. `go vet` prints a parse note for a deliberately broken file under `internal/roles/testdata`.\n\n- **Close-out wakes:**\n  - A done close-out wakes the loops that now have work: `workers`, `reviewers`, `triage`, `merger`, or `reviewfix` plus `workers` for a review-changes round.\n  - A close-out that fails, retries, goes stale or needs a human wakes nothing, and neither does dry-run.\n  - Wakes within the 2s debounce window merge into one tick per loop.\n  - A paused controller still runs nothing on a wake.\n- **Approval watch:**\n  - It polls once a minute (`intervals.approvals`, default and minimum 1m) and takes no slot.\n  - An approved item with no worker label wakes triage.\n  - An item that was `needs-human` or `executor:failed` on the previous poll and no longer is wakes the loops that own it.\n  - Wakes are logged as `controller.wake` with `reason=closeout`, `approval` or `unblocked`.\n  - It is registered as an `approvals` loop and can be selected with `--loops`.\n- **Unblock gap:** GitHub can't search for a removed label, so the unblock watch remembers blocked items in memory. A removal that happens while ard is down is left to the loops' own intervals.\n- **Merger wake:** close-out doesn't mark PRs ready, so I wake the merger on a review `:done` label instead.\n- **Docs:** I updated the \"One pool of job slots\" section of `docs/proposal.md`, its intervals example, and the config table in `docs/site/configuration.md`. I did not edit the triage gate, worker loop and reviewer loop sections separately.\n- **Gate test:** I did not add the plan's triage-gate test (a rejected approval still starts no worker). The gate itself is unchanged.\n\nNew tests cover the config key, the per-outcome wake targets, controller wake behaviour (including coalescing and pause) and the watch. The report is at `.ard/406/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":100959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"output_tokens":730,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9504e90-0a46-4f9b-9664-2e88cac7e920","uuid":"f27cd1d7-c8f8-4d4c-8f6e-a30c23204d5f","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:09:48.729Z","request_id":"req_011ChPnAimN3W1H4AQy9GkNN"}
